  "notes": "Kazakh in Cyrillic script (Kazakhstan official orthography). Eleven-vowel system with front/back and labial harmony (McCollum & Chen 2020). А = central-back /ɑ/ (not front [a]); Ы = central schwa-like /ə/ (not [ɯ]); Ө = mid central rounded /ɵ/. Қ = uvular /q/; Ғ = /ʁ/; Ң = /ŋ/; Ұ = back unrounded /ʊ/; Ү = /y/; І = /ɪ/. Orthographic ⟨и⟩ and ⟨у⟩ represent the phonetically diphthongal /ije̯/ and /uw̯/ nuclei; this spec transcribes them as simple vowels (i, u) pending a positional glide rule. Transitioning to Latin script (phased 2017-2025, not yet complete); this spec covers the Cyrillic orthography, which is what the scored gold sets use.",
